Another good option (especially if your screen still isn’t big enough to fit everything you want) is to use a different graphics device.  It can give you a bit more control over things like this.

The code below uses the PDF device, for example.

Dave

# Tell R to create a PDF file that's 10x10 inches
pdf("example.pdf", width = 10, height = 10)
plot(mtcars) # Make a big plot that might not fit comfortably in RStudio
dev.off() # Seal up the file so it's readable

