Kristina,

With plotting it seems as though it's expecting a vector instead of a list, judging from the error.

As far as data.frame() and expand.grid() giving you the same result, that's what's expected in your case as you're providing a single value for both TRat and Area.  If you were to provide say 2 values for each of  TRat and Area data.frame() would only combine the 1st position values in each vector in the 1st row and the 2nd values in the 2nd row, whereas expand.grid() would give you all of the combinations thereof.

